WEBVTT

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.680
No, no.

00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:31.944
No, no, it's overheating.

00:00:34.468 --> 00:00:36.427
Come on. Keep it together!

00:00:39.821 --> 00:00:41.910
- Aah!

00:00:41.954 --> 00:00:44.217
Sorry.

00:01:59.597 --> 00:02:03.688
&lt;i&gt;
Captain's log, stardate 58354.2.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:03.731 --> 00:02:06.212
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is back
at Tulgana IV,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:06.256 --> 00:02:07.822
&lt;i&gt;where we'll be updating&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:07.866 --> 00:02:09.650
&lt;i&gt;the Federation consulate's
power systems,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:09.694 --> 00:02:12.479
&lt;i&gt;a straightforward job
which gives us extra time&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:12.523 --> 00:02:15.047
&lt;i&gt;to fill some of our
Starfleet quotas.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.180
Ugh, the recruitment booth, no!

00:02:17.223 --> 00:02:19.617
- Well, someone's got to do it.
- Uh, do they?

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.445
'Cause last time I checked,
nobody's ever signed up

00:02:21.488 --> 00:02:23.229
for Starfleet
at the recruitment booth.

00:02:23.273 --> 00:02:24.752
- I did.
- Shh, shh, you're not helping.

00:02:24.796 --> 00:02:26.711
- Sorry.
- I know it's not super exciting,

00:02:26.754 --> 00:02:28.800
but it's our assignment.
What are you gonna do?

00:02:28.843 --> 00:02:31.194
Hmm, complain the whole time
and make it twice as miserable.

00:02:31.237 --> 00:02:34.022
That is your specialty.

00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:36.329
Ow.

00:02:36.373 --> 00:02:38.505
You okay, Rutherford?
Man, you look wiped.

00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:39.985
I haven't slept in a week.

00:02:40.028 --> 00:02:41.552
I keep having
the same crazy nightmare.

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:43.336
Ooh, the one where you're
in a new timeline

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:44.729
with Kirk and Spock

00:02:44.772 --> 00:02:46.121
where they have
cinematic chemistry?

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.123
- Ugh, I wish.
- Looks like you've got

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.038
some long-term memories
stuck in the buffer.

00:02:50.082 --> 00:02:52.519
Probably useless stuff like when
you called the captain "Mom."

00:02:52.563 --> 00:02:54.042
Want me to purge the cache?

00:02:54.086 --> 00:02:56.088
Yes. Anything to help me sleep.

00:02:56.131 --> 00:02:58.133
- And done.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.526
Why don't you go take a nap?

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.962
You'll wake up feeling
like a new man.

00:03:01.006 --> 00:03:02.486
Thanks, Tendi.

00:03:02.529 --> 00:03:04.009
Hope you're right.

00:03:06.098 --> 00:03:08.405
There's a spot where we can set
up in the commuter's market.

00:03:08.448 --> 00:03:10.145
I have a degree
in xenohistory, but sure,

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.539
put me on folding-table duty.
That's great.

00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:15.499
Oh, I'm sorry, is the booth
not exciting enough for you?

00:03:15.542 --> 00:03:16.978
Yeah, actually, it's the worst

00:03:17.022 --> 00:03:18.458
and I'm really glad
you said something.

00:03:18.502 --> 00:03:19.503
Can we get a different
assignment, please?

00:03:19.546 --> 00:03:20.982
I don't care if you like it,

00:03:21.026 --> 00:03:22.288
- that's not the point.
- No. The point is

00:03:22.332 --> 00:03:23.898
to give us work
nobody cares about

00:03:23.942 --> 00:03:26.074
so the captain can tick off
a meaningless box.

00:03:26.118 --> 00:03:28.642
I care, and I'm gonna be
checking in today.

00:03:28.686 --> 00:03:31.602
If you so much as step
one foot out of that booth,

00:03:31.645 --> 00:03:34.257
I will transfer you
to Starbase 80.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.693
Starbase 80?

00:03:35.736 --> 00:03:37.303
Don't joke about that.
Starbase 80 is the worst.

00:03:37.347 --> 00:03:39.523
When I get down there,
you better be in the booth

00:03:39.566 --> 00:03:41.481
with a PADD full
of contact info,

00:03:41.525 --> 00:03:42.917
or you'll be at SB80

00:03:42.961 --> 00:03:44.484
faster than you can
possibly imagine.

00:03:44.528 --> 00:03:46.269
Okay, okay, I get it.

00:03:55.495 --> 00:03:57.932
Okey dokey,
time for some shut-eye.

00:03:57.976 --> 00:04:01.066
Hmm.

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:04.461
- Huh?

00:04:04.504 --> 00:04:06.289
Ah, my [bleep] head.

00:04:06.332 --> 00:04:08.552
Did I even go out last night?

00:04:08.595 --> 00:04:11.076
Wait, what's going on here?

00:04:11.119 --> 00:04:15.472
Ugh, those are the ugliest
nacelles I've ever seen.

00:04:15.515 --> 00:04:17.387
And who put
Engineering down there?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.779
That's stupid.

00:04:18.823 --> 00:04:20.955
Wait a minute,
California-class?

00:04:20.999 --> 00:04:22.522
How did I get here?

00:04:22.566 --> 00:04:24.176
&lt;i&gt;
Ensign Samanthan Rutherford.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:24.219 --> 00:04:28.006
&lt;i&gt;Transferred from Douglas Station
on stardate 56329.4.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:28.049 --> 00:04:29.616
Okay, shut up, shut up.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.791
What the hell is this?

00:04:33.011 --> 00:04:34.142
Holy moly.

00:04:34.186 --> 00:04:36.101
What the heck is happening here?

00:04:36.144 --> 00:04:38.321
Hey, hey! Let me out of here.

00:04:38.364 --> 00:04:41.019
Hey, you. Give me back
control of my body.

00:04:41.062 --> 00:04:43.108
Nah, dude, this is my body.

00:04:43.151 --> 00:04:44.370
You already effed it up.

00:04:44.414 --> 00:04:46.024
- No, it's not.
- Whatever, man.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.808
I don't take orders
from a reflection.

00:04:47.852 --> 00:04:49.375
I'm not a reflection.

00:04:49.419 --> 00:04:52.335
Help! I think an anaphasic alien
took over my body.

00:04:52.378 --> 00:04:55.033
- You're an anaphasic alien.
- Nuh-uh, you are.

00:04:55.076 --> 00:04:56.469
Hey, what is this thing
on my face?

00:04:56.513 --> 00:04:57.688
It's my face.

00:04:57.731 --> 00:04:59.080
Fine, fine, fine,
don't answer it.

00:04:59.124 --> 00:05:01.692
- I don't need you.
- Hey, hey! Get back here!

00:05:01.735 --> 00:05:02.997
Aw, man.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.617
Starfleet, get your Starfleet.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.140
We got new worlds,

00:05:15.183 --> 00:05:16.968
they're strange,
and they need seeking out.

00:05:17.011 --> 00:05:20.058
Wow, it's crazy to hear you,
like, actually trying.

00:05:20.101 --> 00:05:22.060
Yeah, I have to.
Ransom's got it out for me.

00:05:22.103 --> 00:05:24.192
I'm not taking any chances
with creepy-ass Starbase 80.

00:05:24.236 --> 00:05:27.935
Do you have to go to Starfleet
Academy to work on a ship?

00:05:27.979 --> 00:05:29.502
Ah, thank you for asking.
No, not at all.

00:05:29.546 --> 00:05:30.895
You can enlist as an NCO
and then go

00:05:30.938 --> 00:05:32.287
to the Tech Services
Academy on Mars.

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:33.332
You could work
in a transporter bay.

00:05:33.376 --> 00:05:34.333
How about that?

00:05:34.377 --> 00:05:36.074
Really?

00:05:36.117 --> 00:05:37.815
Do the transporter guys
ever get to sit on the bridge?

00:05:37.858 --> 00:05:40.339
Um, I mean, yeah, I guess,
it could... it could happen.

00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:42.123
Hey, pal.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:44.517
You're signing up for seven
years in a windowless room.

00:05:44.561 --> 00:05:46.389
Wait, really?

00:05:46.432 --> 00:05:48.260
Don't listen to her, the ships
have, like, tons of windows.

00:05:48.303 --> 00:05:49.566
It's, like, practically
a greenhouse, right?

00:05:49.609 --> 00:05:50.871
Just not, like,
every single room.

00:05:50.915 --> 00:05:52.482
- Meh.
- Ugh.

00:05:52.525 --> 00:05:54.397
What the hell, lady?
I was about to close.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.834
Aw, did I step on your
little sales pitch?

00:05:56.877 --> 00:05:59.445
What are you even, some
kind of space archaeologist?

00:05:59.489 --> 00:06:01.491
Independent space archaeologist.

00:06:01.534 --> 00:06:03.449
That first part's important,
since you know,

00:06:03.493 --> 00:06:06.147
I'm free to do whatever I want,

00:06:06.191 --> 00:06:08.323
unlike some ensigns
around here.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.673
All right, fine. Whatever.

00:06:09.716 --> 00:06:12.284
Uh, Starfleet.
Get your Starfleet.

00:06:12.327 --> 00:06:14.460
Prepare yourself
for Warp 10 excitement.

00:06:14.504 --> 00:06:16.767
Discover
the undiscovered country.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.552
How often do you get
to collect dilithium?

00:06:19.596 --> 00:06:21.336
Oh, all the time,
tons of crystals.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.642
Hey, buddy.

00:06:22.686 --> 00:06:24.427
- You want to be a Borg?
- What? No.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:27.299
Starfleet crews get assimilated
all the time.

00:06:27.342 --> 00:06:30.084
Hope you like being covered
in black rubber tubing.

00:06:30.128 --> 00:06:32.522
- Aah!
-  We do not!

00:06:32.565 --> 00:06:35.481
Borg drone, Starfleet drone,
what's the diff?

00:06:35.525 --> 00:06:37.570
The "diff" is I'm about to shove
one of those artifacts

00:06:37.614 --> 00:06:38.832
- up your ass.
- Mariner, don't.

00:06:38.876 --> 00:06:40.094
- Just stay focused.

00:06:43.358 --> 00:06:45.012
Graphenated corridor joists?

00:06:45.056 --> 00:06:48.059
These Cali-class junkers
are such fire traps.

00:06:48.102 --> 00:06:51.497
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is a great ship.
Give me back my body.

00:06:51.541 --> 00:06:53.281
Hey, there, pretty lady.

00:06:53.325 --> 00:06:55.458
- Hey, Rutherford. What's up?
- No, no. Don't talk to her.

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:57.938
I mean, everything,
now that I ran into you.

00:06:57.982 --> 00:07:00.158
Trill, huh?
Those spots go all the way down?

00:07:00.201 --> 00:07:01.899
Excuse me?

00:07:01.942 --> 00:07:04.162
Barnes, call the captain.
He's an alien or something.

00:07:04.205 --> 00:07:06.512
Hey, Trill, uh, when is
the security shift change?

00:07:06.556 --> 00:07:07.513
Why would I know?

00:07:07.557 --> 00:07:09.167
Because you're in security?

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:10.734
We've been on four dates

00:07:10.777 --> 00:07:12.605
and you don't even know
what division I'm in?

00:07:12.649 --> 00:07:14.172
Well, damn. Maybe if you
weren't so boring,

00:07:14.215 --> 00:07:15.608
I'd remember some of this stuff.

00:07:15.652 --> 00:07:17.131
Uh!

00:07:17.175 --> 00:07:18.698
- Oh, okay. Walk away.

00:07:18.742 --> 00:07:20.744
I got to figure out a way
to contact Tendi.

00:07:20.787 --> 00:07:22.397
She'll know
how to get rid of you.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:23.398
Wait, who's Tendi?

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:25.531
Uh, nobody. Never mind.

00:07:25.575 --> 00:07:27.794
- Computer, locate Tendi.
- Computer, no!

00:07:27.838 --> 00:07:29.535
&lt;i&gt;Ensign Tendi
is currently located&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:29.579 --> 00:07:31.232
&lt;i&gt;in Repair Bay Five.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:31.276 --> 00:07:32.843
No, no, no, no. I-I don't know
what you're thinking,

00:07:32.886 --> 00:07:34.540
but you stay away from her.

00:07:35.585 --> 00:07:38.022
Hey, check out this pod plant
from Omicron Ceti III.

00:07:38.065 --> 00:07:40.198
It blasts out
mind-control pollen.

00:07:40.241 --> 00:07:41.504
Jeepers creepers.

00:07:41.547 --> 00:07:42.722
That's swell.

00:07:42.766 --> 00:07:44.419
I don't even talk like that.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.160
She's gonna see right
through you, you goofy goof.

00:07:46.204 --> 00:07:47.858
Oopsie doodle.

00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:49.990
I can't remember when
the security shift change is.

00:07:50.034 --> 00:07:52.906
-  It's at 0900, silly.
- Of course.

00:07:54.038 --> 00:07:55.648
Tendi, come on. That's not me.

00:07:58.172 --> 00:07:59.260
Ah! Damn.

00:07:59.304 --> 00:08:00.610
It worked.

00:08:00.653 --> 00:08:02.525
Dude, don't do that.
This is my body.

00:08:02.568 --> 00:08:03.569
Who are you talking to?

00:08:03.613 --> 00:08:05.092
Don't do this?

00:08:05.136 --> 00:08:07.051
- Aah! I'll kill you.

00:08:07.094 --> 00:08:09.096
Rutherford, are you okay?

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.837
Let me take a look
at your implant.

00:08:10.881 --> 00:08:11.882
Get away from me!

00:08:11.925 --> 00:08:13.318
- I'm fine!
- Aah!

00:08:13.361 --> 00:08:15.886
:
Ensign Tendi to sickbay.

00:08:15.929 --> 00:08:18.628
I need an emergency
medical team on Deck 11.

00:08:18.671 --> 00:08:20.151
Huh.

00:08:20.194 --> 00:08:21.631
See more
where that came from, kid.

00:08:21.674 --> 00:08:22.719
Just join the Indie
Archaeologists' Guild.

00:08:23.807 --> 00:08:25.156
More like space thieves.

00:08:25.199 --> 00:08:26.636
Hey, why don't you go
in that museum

00:08:26.679 --> 00:08:28.289
and steal some artifacts?
I know you want to.

00:08:28.333 --> 00:08:30.161
:
Oh, right.

00:08:30.204 --> 00:08:32.119
Because everyone who doesn't
salute their boss

00:08:32.163 --> 00:08:33.643
is a criminal?

00:08:33.686 --> 00:08:35.862
You know, lady,
if you are really dedicated

00:08:35.906 --> 00:08:37.298
to the pursuit of knowledge,

00:08:37.342 --> 00:08:38.648
then you're kind of
limiting yourself

00:08:38.691 --> 00:08:39.997
by not being
in Starfleet, actually.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.390
Ooh, actually,
I was in Starfleet.

00:08:42.434 --> 00:08:44.915
Petra Aberdeen--
graduated Academy,

00:08:44.958 --> 00:08:46.133
did a tour in the fleet

00:08:46.177 --> 00:08:47.831
before wising up
and getting out.

00:08:47.874 --> 00:08:49.310
- Whoa.

00:08:49.354 --> 00:08:51.095
You served on the &lt;i&gt;Victory?&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:51.138 --> 00:08:53.227
Well, you must have screwed up
pretty bad to end up here.

00:08:53.271 --> 00:08:55.969
Sure, why leave
the big fancy ships,

00:08:56.013 --> 00:08:58.450
just for a life of freedom
and nonviolence?

00:08:58.493 --> 00:09:00.234
Starfleet isn't violent.

00:09:00.278 --> 00:09:02.672
Well, tell that to the Romulans,
the Klingons, the Cardassians...

00:09:02.715 --> 00:09:04.587
What? They attack us.
It's self-defense.

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:07.938
Oh, right, you guys totally
aren't a pseudo navy at all.

00:09:10.157 --> 00:09:12.551
- Aah!

00:09:17.077 --> 00:09:18.122
Ah!

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:25.956
Oh, come on, come on, come on!

00:09:25.999 --> 00:09:27.740
Tulgana IV has an ion field,

00:09:27.784 --> 00:09:29.873
transporter won't get
a solid lock.

00:09:29.916 --> 00:09:34.051
You know that, baby bear.
Unless you aren't you.

00:09:34.094 --> 00:09:36.140
My nickname's "baby bear"?
That's stupid.

00:09:39.883 --> 00:09:41.493
Aah!

00:09:42.929 --> 00:09:45.671
Oh, here we are.
Captain's yacht.

00:09:45.715 --> 00:09:47.499
- Now we're talking.
- You messed

00:09:47.542 --> 00:09:48.979
with the wrong crew, buddy.

00:09:49.022 --> 00:09:50.807
Oh, yeah? Then why am I
about to take off

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:52.678
with my own
warp-capable starship?

00:09:52.722 --> 00:09:53.810
They'll never find me.

00:09:53.853 --> 00:09:56.421
Unless someone buys them
some time.

00:09:59.685 --> 00:10:02.079
Man, I'll kill you.
Don't touch that.

00:10:02.122 --> 00:10:04.864
- Fine, I don't need to anyway.
- Wait. Really?

00:10:04.908 --> 00:10:06.257
Sorry, baby bear.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.562
Aah!

00:10:11.654 --> 00:10:13.220
Dr. T'Ana, I need a medical team

00:10:13.264 --> 00:10:15.658
to the captain's yacht now!

00:10:21.968 --> 00:10:23.666
Huh.

00:10:23.709 --> 00:10:25.972
According to my scans,
there's no anaphasic presence.

00:10:26.016 --> 00:10:28.061
Ensign Rutherford
is still himself,

00:10:28.105 --> 00:10:31.325
but his memory and personality
are from a decade ago.

00:10:31.369 --> 00:10:34.154
It's almost like a backup
overwrote his brain.

00:10:34.198 --> 00:10:36.330
I-I cleared the cache
on his implant.

00:10:36.374 --> 00:10:38.376
Did I erase my best friend?

00:10:38.419 --> 00:10:42.032
Oh, cerebral activity's high.
Something's going on in there.

00:10:42.075 --> 00:10:44.948
We'll just have to wait and see
which Rutherford wakes up.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.868
Wha...?

00:10:51.911 --> 00:10:53.652
Oh, come on, man.

00:10:53.696 --> 00:10:56.046
Yep, now we're both stuck
in a blank white void.

00:10:56.089 --> 00:10:58.091
Just shut up, old man.
This is all your fault.

00:10:58.135 --> 00:10:59.484
Wait.

00:10:59.527 --> 00:11:01.007
You're a younger version of me.

00:11:01.051 --> 00:11:03.880
No, you're the older,
cornier version of me.

00:11:03.923 --> 00:11:05.751
And now we're both stuck
in the stupid mindscape.

00:11:05.795 --> 00:11:07.187
Mind what?

00:11:07.231 --> 00:11:10.016
It's a manifestation
of our brain. Look.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.323
See? Try it out.

00:11:14.804 --> 00:11:16.370
Whoa.

00:11:16.414 --> 00:11:17.763
Damn, you're right.

00:11:17.807 --> 00:11:19.112
This says we're
in my subconscious.

00:11:19.156 --> 00:11:20.723
Yeah, dummy.

00:11:20.766 --> 00:11:22.246
The brain can't handle having
two full copies

00:11:22.289 --> 00:11:24.465
- of a person in here.
- So it partitioned us?

00:11:24.509 --> 00:11:27.294
Until one emerges as the
dominant personality, yeah.

00:11:27.338 --> 00:11:29.166
Well, that's me.
You're an imposter.

00:11:29.209 --> 00:11:31.124
Oh, really?
Then why can I do this?

00:11:33.561 --> 00:11:34.519
Wait.

00:11:34.562 --> 00:11:35.999
I've been here before.

00:11:36.042 --> 00:11:37.000
Oh.

00:11:37.043 --> 00:11:39.002
What's this?

00:11:39.045 --> 00:11:41.047
The &lt;i&gt;Sampaguita,&lt;/i&gt;
fastest racer in the quadrant,

00:11:41.091 --> 00:11:42.875
designed by yours truly.

00:11:42.919 --> 00:11:44.485
This isn't a ship,

00:11:44.529 --> 00:11:46.009
this is a seat strapped
to an impulse engine.

00:11:46.052 --> 00:11:47.619
Yeah, baby. Pretty cool, right?

00:11:47.662 --> 00:11:49.099
Hang on. If you're young me,

00:11:49.142 --> 00:11:51.101
why don't
I remember building this?

00:11:51.144 --> 00:11:52.624
Because you erased
your own memories, man.

00:11:52.667 --> 00:11:54.626
And you did it to me with this.

00:11:54.669 --> 00:11:56.236
My implant? No way.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.064
It was just to help me
with engineering.

00:11:58.108 --> 00:11:59.936
You sure about that?

00:12:01.546 --> 00:12:03.809
What if someone asks
why he has it?

00:12:03.853 --> 00:12:06.551
We programmed that in.
He'll think it was elective.

00:12:06.594 --> 00:12:09.510
You tried to erase all
the memories that made us cool,

00:12:09.554 --> 00:12:10.903
but it didn't work.

00:12:10.947 --> 00:12:12.296
The brain is
more complicated than that

00:12:12.339 --> 00:12:14.515
and it kept my cool ass
stored away.

00:12:14.559 --> 00:12:16.604
So, blao, here I am, baby.

00:12:16.648 --> 00:12:18.084
If that's true,
then how come you never tried

00:12:18.128 --> 00:12:19.085
to take over before?

00:12:19.129 --> 00:12:20.826
I did, dude.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.697
Haven't you noticed this thing
is always bugging out?

00:12:22.741 --> 00:12:24.395
Your programs turning
against you?

00:12:24.438 --> 00:12:27.050
- Behavioral shifts?
- I did like pears for a minute.

00:12:27.093 --> 00:12:29.835
I love pears. That was me
trying to get my body back.

00:12:29.879 --> 00:12:32.969
Fine, so we're both us--
I mean me.

00:12:33.012 --> 00:12:35.232
But if you take over,
won't I get erased?

00:12:35.275 --> 00:12:37.321
Yeah. Only one of us
can walk out of here.

00:12:37.364 --> 00:12:38.409
We have to choose.

00:12:39.845 --> 00:12:40.890
And I choose me.

00:12:40.933 --> 00:12:42.413
Later, loser.

00:12:48.245 --> 00:12:49.246
Come on.

00:12:49.289 --> 00:12:50.856
Get off me, man.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:53.728
You're not going anywhere
until we figure this out.

00:12:53.772 --> 00:12:54.991
What is this place anyway?

00:12:55.034 --> 00:12:56.383
This is our garage, man.

00:12:56.427 --> 00:12:57.994
We used to sneak off
from the Academy

00:12:58.037 --> 00:13:00.039
to build our
sick racing ships here.

00:13:00.083 --> 00:13:01.475
That's cool,
but why the sneaking?

00:13:01.519 --> 00:13:03.173
Because of stupid Starfleet.

00:13:03.216 --> 00:13:04.827
They never let us test
our own engines.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:06.741
They wanted to make us wait
until we graduated

00:13:06.785 --> 00:13:09.222
before we're even near
a warp core. So dumb.

00:13:09.266 --> 00:13:11.050
Makes sense.

00:13:11.094 --> 00:13:12.704
We could have gotten hurt
messing around with this stuff.

00:13:12.747 --> 00:13:14.314
Oh, but we did more
than mess around.

00:13:14.358 --> 00:13:15.750
We funded all this

00:13:15.794 --> 00:13:17.709
by winning Devron races, baby.

00:13:17.752 --> 00:13:19.102
Those go through
the neutral zone.

00:13:19.145 --> 00:13:20.277
They're illegal.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.582
Yeah, duh.

00:13:21.626 --> 00:13:23.062
Man, you really bought
into that

00:13:23.106 --> 00:13:24.629
whole okey dokey bull[bleep],
didn't you?

00:13:24.672 --> 00:13:26.761
Yes.

00:13:26.805 --> 00:13:28.372
We can't stay in here forever.

00:13:28.415 --> 00:13:30.243
Shouldn't the best
engineer get to take control?

00:13:30.287 --> 00:13:33.420
Yes. Great idea.
Let's take an engineering test.

00:13:33.464 --> 00:13:34.987
No, man, tests are dumb.

00:13:35.031 --> 00:13:37.120
How about something
a little more interesting?

00:13:37.163 --> 00:13:40.427
A race. Both of us
build our own ships.

00:13:40.471 --> 00:13:42.342
- Winner takes the brain.
- And the loser?

00:13:42.386 --> 00:13:44.388
Gets erased.
Dude, come on. Keep up.

00:13:44.431 --> 00:13:45.998
Aah!
I don't know how much longer

00:13:46.042 --> 00:13:47.478
our body can
stay in this coma,

00:13:47.521 --> 00:13:49.393
so one of us has to take over.

00:13:50.437 --> 00:13:52.048
Okay, I'm in.

00:13:55.355 --> 00:13:56.966
Do you ever get
to touch mummies?

00:13:57.009 --> 00:13:58.706
Constantly.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.057
And you never have to go
back in time to save Earth.

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:03.886
That only happened, like,
four times. Five, tops.

00:14:03.929 --> 00:14:05.017
Oh, great.

00:14:05.061 --> 00:14:06.323
The Collector's Guild.

00:14:06.366 --> 00:14:08.194
:
Well, look at this.

00:14:08.238 --> 00:14:11.502
Word's getting around you little
ensigns can't leave the booth.

00:14:11.545 --> 00:14:13.634
The only thing
you two collect is dust.

00:14:13.678 --> 00:14:16.463
- Oh, now, that was collectible.

00:14:16.507 --> 00:14:18.639
Yeah, well, that was dumb
and you should hate yourself.

00:14:18.683 --> 00:14:20.293
So there.

00:14:20.337 --> 00:14:21.773
Okay, let's just calm down,
don't listen to them.

00:14:21.816 --> 00:14:23.644
And... Oh, no, here come
the conspiracy truthers.

00:14:23.688 --> 00:14:25.646
Hey, Starfleet, when are we
gonna hear the truth

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:27.300
about what happened to Sisko?

00:14:27.344 --> 00:14:29.737
What? No, he's working hard
in a celestial temple.

00:14:29.781 --> 00:14:30.782
Yeah, right.

00:14:30.825 --> 00:14:32.610
How about when parasites crawled

00:14:32.653 --> 00:14:35.004
into Starfleet admirals' butts
and took over their brains?

00:14:35.047 --> 00:14:36.657
Want to come clean about that?

00:14:36.701 --> 00:14:38.485
It's just a stupid conspiracy.
It never happened.

00:14:38.529 --> 00:14:39.573
Actually, I think it did.

00:14:39.617 --> 00:14:41.053
Really?

00:14:41.097 --> 00:14:43.186
How do we know you two
don't got butt bugs?

00:14:43.229 --> 00:14:45.840
Well, if we did, we'd have
to kill you for figuring it out.

00:14:45.884 --> 00:14:48.408
Sure, if you could
leave the booth.

00:14:50.367 --> 00:14:51.629
- No, no, no, no.

00:14:51.672 --> 00:14:54.066
- Not the &lt;i&gt;'Gazer!&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:11.997 --> 00:15:14.478
Oh, my God!

00:15:14.521 --> 00:15:17.263
Hang on a second,
is this a Starfleet design?

00:15:17.307 --> 00:15:19.091
Yeah. It's the &lt;i&gt;Delta Flyer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:19.135 --> 00:15:21.659
It's superfast and it's got
pop-out impulse thrusters.

00:15:21.702 --> 00:15:23.356
Tom Paris designed
it on &lt;i&gt;Voyager.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:24.836 --> 00:15:26.446
I mean, you could
have built literally

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:28.840
anything you could imagine.
You know that, right?

00:15:28.883 --> 00:15:30.102
I've always wanted one of these.

00:15:30.146 --> 00:15:31.538
It's got some Borg tech and...

00:15:31.582 --> 00:15:33.192
Dude, it's a shuttle
with a paint job.

00:15:33.236 --> 00:15:35.325
You could've made this.

00:15:37.457 --> 00:15:40.373
Whoa-key dokey!

00:15:40.417 --> 00:15:42.201
Vulcan inverters, quad engines,

00:15:42.245 --> 00:15:44.638
I mean, you might as well
just give me the body now.

00:15:44.682 --> 00:15:46.031
Whatever.
The &lt;i&gt;Delta Flyer's&lt;/i&gt; awesome.

00:15:46.075 --> 00:15:47.815
It even came with
a matching outfit for me.

00:15:47.859 --> 00:15:49.643
You know, for a minute there

00:15:49.687 --> 00:15:52.298
I thought maybe the years
you had on me might even us up,

00:15:52.342 --> 00:15:53.952
but this is just sad.

00:15:53.996 --> 00:15:56.172
Hang on.
Let me get my outfit on.

00:15:58.087 --> 00:16:00.698
Whoa, hold on,
you're on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:00.741 --> 00:16:02.961
Your captain bombed
the Pakleds, didn't she?

00:16:03.005 --> 00:16:05.790
Oh! There were so many
good artifacts in that city.

00:16:05.833 --> 00:16:07.835
What?
Those idiots bombed themselves!

00:16:07.879 --> 00:16:09.750
Great diplomacy either way.

00:16:09.794 --> 00:16:11.578
Oh, no. No, no, no.

00:16:11.622 --> 00:16:13.276
I'm not [bleep]ing doing this.

00:16:13.319 --> 00:16:15.060
I don't want to hear it
from you outpost scientists.

00:16:15.104 --> 00:16:17.236
Well, I have a question
about joining Starfleet.

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:18.977
Oh. Uh, really?

00:16:19.021 --> 00:16:22.241
Yeah, I love those uniforms.
If I join, do I get one?

00:16:22.285 --> 00:16:23.851
Yeah. Yeah, you do.

00:16:23.895 --> 00:16:25.244
I mean, our style isn't across
the whole fleet,

00:16:25.288 --> 00:16:26.724
but they're in
the California-class...

00:16:26.767 --> 00:16:28.856
God, I'm so sorry, I-I can't.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.163
This guy actually thinks
the uniforms are cool.

00:16:31.207 --> 00:16:32.599
They are cool.

00:16:32.643 --> 00:16:34.645
Uh, then why are they
always changing?

00:16:34.688 --> 00:16:36.038
Starfleet updates them.

00:16:36.081 --> 00:16:37.430
There's always room
for improvement.

00:16:37.474 --> 00:16:38.953
Like-like we get
this really cool flap.

00:16:38.997 --> 00:16:40.999
Oh, please.
Why do you even need uniforms?

00:16:41.043 --> 00:16:42.392
You are not in the military.

00:16:42.435 --> 00:16:44.133
- I'd say they are.
- Oh, shut up!

00:16:44.176 --> 00:16:46.526
Us outpost scientists
wear whatever we want.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.528
Like this belt.
Can you wear a belt?

00:16:48.572 --> 00:16:49.834
Ha.

00:16:49.877 --> 00:16:50.878
- They can wear jewelry.

00:16:50.922 --> 00:16:51.966
Oops.

00:16:54.926 --> 00:16:56.406
- That was my rank pip!

00:16:58.451 --> 00:17:00.149
Whoa, okay. Boims, calm down.

00:17:00.192 --> 00:17:01.280
We can replicate you another
one. You don't have to...

00:17:01.324 --> 00:17:02.629
Aah!

00:17:02.673 --> 00:17:05.023
Without Starfleet
none of you would exist!

00:17:05.067 --> 00:17:08.200
We don't want to protect you
from the Klingons and the Borg.

00:17:08.244 --> 00:17:11.247
We just want to explore
and study [bleep]ing quasars!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.075
But you know what?
It's the right thing to do!

00:17:13.771 --> 00:17:16.078
Dude, get back in the booth.
What if Ransom shows up?

00:17:16.121 --> 00:17:18.080
Stupid [bleep]ing truthers!
You hate the truth!

00:17:18.123 --> 00:17:20.691
You're just a bunch
of pathetic gossipy weirdos!

00:17:20.734 --> 00:17:22.040
Collecting is stupid!

00:17:22.084 --> 00:17:23.215
It doesn't make you happy!

00:17:23.259 --> 00:17:25.957
Your ships smell like ass!

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.654
Boimler, get back here.

00:17:27.698 --> 00:17:29.613
You're always getting people
trapped inside of games.

00:17:29.656 --> 00:17:31.528
Stop trapping people
inside of games!

00:17:32.616 --> 00:17:33.965
Is that guy with you?

00:17:34.008 --> 00:17:36.533
Yes, but, uh, that
behavior is not...

00:17:36.576 --> 00:17:39.144
If being in Starfleet gives you
that kind of confidence,

00:17:39.188 --> 00:17:40.450
then I want in.

00:17:40.493 --> 00:17:43.279
He just told a Ferengi
to [bleep].

00:17:43.322 --> 00:17:45.019
- Oh, yes.

00:17:45.063 --> 00:17:46.543
Um, hey, do you like
engineering?

00:17:46.586 --> 00:17:49.415
Uh, love it.
You guys do that kind of stuff?

00:17:49.459 --> 00:17:51.548
Oh, absolutely. They got
a whole division for it.

00:17:51.591 --> 00:17:54.116
The Doctor didn't spend seven
years in the Delta Quadrant

00:17:54.159 --> 00:17:55.769
for you [bleep]s
to question his agency.

00:17:55.813 --> 00:17:56.901
He's got rights.

00:18:01.732 --> 00:18:03.516
&lt;i&gt;
Man, this is gonna be too easy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.170
&lt;i&gt;I've randomized the route&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:05.214 --> 00:18:06.954
&lt;i&gt;to give you a chance but,
fair warning,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:06.998 --> 00:18:09.522
if you see any Romulans, run.
They don't [bleep] around.

00:18:09.566 --> 00:18:11.176
&lt;i&gt;
That's Neutral Zone 101.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:13.004
&lt;i&gt;Oh, okay. Cool, cool.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:13.047 --> 00:18:15.311
&lt;i&gt;So you know all about
the uncharted black holes,&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:15.354 --> 00:18:17.139
&lt;i&gt;rogue planets
and dangerous nebulas?&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:17.182 --> 00:18:18.575
Rogue planets?

00:18:18.618 --> 00:18:20.185
&lt;i&gt;
See you at the finish line, fam.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:20.229 --> 00:18:21.273
&lt;i&gt;Or maybe I won't.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:26.757 --> 00:18:28.367
&lt;i&gt;Ooh, baby. [laughs]&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:28.411 --> 00:18:29.455
&lt;i&gt;Yeah, yeah, yeah.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:35.069 --> 00:18:37.942
&lt;i&gt;Here we go. [whoops]&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:49.258 --> 00:18:50.346
Yeah!

00:18:51.303 --> 00:18:52.478
Punch it, baby, punch it.

00:18:54.176 --> 00:18:55.525
- Aah!

00:18:55.568 --> 00:18:56.961
Told you that Starfleet
made you soft.

00:18:57.004 --> 00:18:59.006
- Oh, [bleep].

00:19:02.575 --> 00:19:03.663
Aah!

00:19:17.199 --> 00:19:18.200
Aah!

00:19:20.376 --> 00:19:22.116
Last man standing
takes all, bruh.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:23.944
&lt;i&gt;
Reroute power to aft shields.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:23.988 --> 00:19:26.164
&lt;i&gt;Let's put some space
between us and that cruiser.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:26.208 --> 00:19:27.861
Ha. What, are you
talking to yourself?

00:19:27.905 --> 00:19:29.907
Nope. Talking to my crew.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:32.257
I boosted shields to 130%,
Captain.

00:19:32.301 --> 00:19:33.780
Charting a course
through that debris field.

00:19:33.824 --> 00:19:35.956
- It should provide cover.
- We've got this.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.654
&lt;i&gt;
Wait, hold up. Who is that?&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:37.697 --> 00:19:39.830
We used our imagination
to make anything we wanted,

00:19:39.873 --> 00:19:41.614
and I wasn't gonna race
without my friends.

00:19:41.658 --> 00:19:43.007
Man, that ain't fair.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:44.661
&lt;i&gt;
You said anything goes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:44.704 --> 00:19:46.445
Aah!

00:19:47.446 --> 00:19:48.447
All right, Mariner.

00:19:48.491 --> 00:19:49.753
You better be in that booth

00:19:49.796 --> 00:19:51.276
with a PADD full of names, or...

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:53.017
Great. Okay. So, yeah,
you filled it all out?

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:54.236
- Fantastic.
- Don't doubt me!

00:19:54.279 --> 00:19:55.585
I failed the Kobayashi Maru

00:19:55.628 --> 00:19:57.587
- 17 times, mother[bleep]!
- Boimler?

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.110
What the hell is going on?

00:19:59.153 --> 00:20:01.460
I think that guy's being
controlled by butt bugs.

00:20:01.504 --> 00:20:03.549
Ah, [bleep] off!

00:20:12.341 --> 00:20:13.342
Aah!

00:20:15.344 --> 00:20:17.607
His shields are down.
He's not gonna make it.

00:20:20.218 --> 00:20:21.872
Tendi, now!

00:20:25.832 --> 00:20:28.835
- I got him.

00:20:28.879 --> 00:20:30.620
Hey. You're okay, you're safe.

00:20:30.663 --> 00:20:31.664
What are you doing?

00:20:31.708 --> 00:20:33.231
Mariner, get us out of here.

00:20:33.275 --> 00:20:34.450
Okey dokey.

00:20:41.195 --> 00:20:42.240
You won.

00:20:46.723 --> 00:20:49.160
I guess Starfleet
taught you something after all.

00:20:49.203 --> 00:20:50.814
No, no, no, don't, no,
don't say that.

00:20:50.857 --> 00:20:53.338
Just hang in there, okay?
You're gon-you're gonna be okay.

00:20:53.382 --> 00:20:55.427
We just need to...
engineer a solution.

00:20:58.169 --> 00:21:01.346
I was always so angry,
at everything.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:05.176
But you-- all that rage is gone.

00:21:05.219 --> 00:21:06.873
Well, can't we merge
and just be both of us,

00:21:06.917 --> 00:21:08.527
all our memories combined?

00:21:08.571 --> 00:21:10.747
Nah. Then we'd both be gone.

00:21:11.878 --> 00:21:14.011
Sometimes it's better to grow.

00:21:15.578 --> 00:21:18.407
I-I just remembered
how we got the implant.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.234
Remember...

00:21:21.192 --> 00:21:23.325
We thought we could do anything.

00:21:23.368 --> 00:21:24.326
Damn it, no.

00:21:24.369 --> 00:21:26.589
Come on, keep it together.

00:21:27.416 --> 00:21:28.460
Aah!

00:21:30.767 --> 00:21:32.638
This is going
to set us back years.

00:21:34.597 --> 00:21:36.381
How much do you want to erase?

00:21:36.425 --> 00:21:38.340
Everything that has
to do with me or the program.

00:21:38.383 --> 00:21:40.037
That's a lot.

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:41.386
He'll come out with a totally
different personality.

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:42.909
I don't care.

00:21:42.953 --> 00:21:44.824
What do we do if someone asks
why he has it?

00:21:44.868 --> 00:21:46.957
We programmed that in.
He'll think it was elective.

00:21:49.176 --> 00:21:50.787
My implant was a coverup?

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:53.920
I guess someone broke
even more rules than we did.

00:21:55.226 --> 00:21:56.619
No. Just hang on.

00:21:56.662 --> 00:21:58.795
We can transfer you into
a positronic brain or...

00:21:58.838 --> 00:22:01.014
No, no. This is right.

00:22:01.058 --> 00:22:04.278
Don't lose those friends.

00:22:04.322 --> 00:22:07.194
Thanks for one last race.

00:22:25.474 --> 00:22:26.910
Huh?

00:22:26.953 --> 00:22:28.390
Take it slow, Ensign.

00:22:28.433 --> 00:22:30.957
- You're gonna be all right.
- Rutherford?

00:22:31.001 --> 00:22:32.481
Are... are you...

00:22:32.524 --> 00:22:34.831
Yeah. I'm okey dokey.

00:22:42.186 --> 00:22:43.753
&lt;i&gt;
I meant what I said, Ensign.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:43.796 --> 00:22:46.146
You knowingly disobeyed
a direct order.

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:47.757
Are you gonna send me
to Starbase 80?

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:49.498
Oh, God, no.
That place is a hellhole.

00:22:49.541 --> 00:22:52.370
Coltar, when he drowned
in the swamp.

00:22:52.414 --> 00:22:53.850
You're just gonna
spend a night in the brig.

00:22:53.893 --> 00:22:56.461
Wow. I've never been
sent to the brig before.

00:22:56.505 --> 00:22:58.289
I hope you don't think
less of me.

00:22:58.332 --> 00:23:00.422
Honestly, hearing you
stand up for Starfleet

00:23:00.465 --> 00:23:02.162
and give it
to those loudmouths--

00:23:02.206 --> 00:23:03.947
- I was impressed.
- Really?

00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:06.340
Oh, yeah. Let's grab a drink
when you're out.

00:23:06.384 --> 00:23:08.473
I want to hear how
those outpost losers cried

00:23:08.517 --> 00:23:10.693
when you
kicked over their table.

00:23:13.391 --> 00:23:15.393
So there's someone out there
who blew you up?

00:23:15.437 --> 00:23:18.135
Yeah, and whoever it was
must have been a higher-up

00:23:18.178 --> 00:23:20.311
in Starfleet back
when I was a first-year,

00:23:20.354 --> 00:23:21.660
but that doesn't
really narrow it down.

00:23:21.704 --> 00:23:23.183
It could have been anybody.

00:23:23.227 --> 00:23:25.011
Dang, I'm sorry
you're in the brig, Boims.

00:23:25.055 --> 00:23:27.100
But thanks for keeping me
from losing my cool today.

00:23:27.144 --> 00:23:28.885
I don't know how
you kept it together.

00:23:28.928 --> 00:23:30.974
That archaeologist
was just so full of it.

00:23:31.017 --> 00:23:33.498
Well, I guess for once
I have to do the mission log.

00:23:33.542 --> 00:23:35.457
Aw, lucky.
That's my favorite part.

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:37.633
:
Of course it is.

00:23:37.676 --> 00:23:39.504
But with Commander Ransom there,

00:23:39.548 --> 00:23:41.375
the situation
de-escalated quickly.

00:23:41.419 --> 00:23:42.942
Next time, recommend
the Starfleet booth

00:23:42.986 --> 00:23:45.510
not be set up near
the following organizations:

00:23:45.554 --> 00:23:47.338
- The Collector's Guild...

00:23:47.381 --> 00:23:48.339
Wow.

00:23:48.382 --> 00:23:49.383
No, thank you.

00:23:49.427 --> 00:23:50.515
&lt;i&gt;Wait, don't hang up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:50.559 --> 00:23:52.125
&lt;i&gt;- You were right.&lt;/i&gt;
- About what?

00:23:52.169 --> 00:23:53.997
&lt;i&gt;I was only being
a pain in the ass&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:56.521
&lt;i&gt;because I needed a distraction
so I could emancipate&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:56.565 --> 00:23:59.306
&lt;i&gt;this little guy
from that crooked museum.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:01.439
&lt;i&gt;Stolen from the Grand Nagus.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:01.483 --> 00:24:03.528
&lt;i&gt;They're offering
quite the reward.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:03.572 --> 00:24:06.531
- Cool story. What do you want? &lt;i&gt;
- I asked around about you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:06.575 --> 00:24:08.577
&lt;i&gt;And I get
that you love Starfleet,&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:08.620 --> 00:24:10.622
&lt;i&gt;but you really have
the potential for more.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:10.666 --> 00:24:13.364
&lt;i&gt;So, you know, if you ever feel
like the bureaucracy&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:13.407 --> 00:24:15.627
&lt;i&gt;is holding you back,
give me a call.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:15.671 --> 00:24:17.499
Uh, yeah, right.
I think I'll be fine.

00:24:17.542 --> 00:24:18.543
&lt;i&gt;I know you will.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:18.587 --> 00:24:20.197
&lt;i&gt;Hang in there, Starfleet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:33.662 --> 00:25:37.662
Chirp.
